.Sh DESCRIPTION
libcmc checks protocol logic written as pure C step functions.
The product calls those functions to run the protocol; libcmc links the
same object files and explores every order in which messages, timers,
disk writes, client requests and crashes can reach them.
.Xr cmc 7
describes the model, and
.Xr cmc 1
the command line.
.Pp
A program supplies three things:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
A
.Vt CmcCore :
the step code and the size of a node's state.
.It
A
.Vt CmcModel :
a core plus the properties to check against it.
.It
A
.Fn main
that calls
.Fn cmc_main ,
or that drives
.Fn cmc_run_new
and
.Fn cmc_check
itself.
.El
.Ss The core
.Bd -literal
typedef struct CmcCore {
	const char *name;
	size_t	state_size;	/* bytes per node */
	size_t	durable_size;	/* leading bytes that survive a crash */
	size_t	cfg_size;	/* at most 256 */
	void	(*cfg_default)(void *cfg);
	int	(*cfg_set)(void *cfg, const char *key, const char *val);
	int	(*nnodes)(const void *cfg);
	void	(*init)(const void *cfg, int node, void *state);
	void	(*step)(const void *cfg, int node, void *state,
		    const CmcEvent *ev, CmcOut *out);
	void	(*apply_persist)(const void *cfg, int node, void *durable,
		    const uint8_t *body, uint16_t len);
	void	(*describe)(const void *cfg, int node, const void *state,
		    FILE *f);			/* optional */
	void	(*describe_msg)(const void *cfg, const uint8_t *body,
		    FILE *f);			/* optional */
	int	(*direct_actions)(const void *cfg, const void *state,
		    CmcAction *acts, int max);	/* calibration only */
	void	(*describe_action)(const void *cfg, CmcAction a,
		    FILE *f);			/* calibration only */
	int	(*clients)(const void *cfg, int node);	/* optional */
} CmcCore;
.Ed
.Pp
A node's state is
.Fa state_size
bytes, fixed, with no pointers.
The engine copies, compares and hashes it as bytes, so the core keeps
it canonical: padding and unused slots zeroed, sets sorted.
.Pp
.Fn cfg_default
fills the core's settings;
.Fn cfg_set
applies one
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
and returns 0, or \-1 to reject it.
.Fn nnodes
returns the number of nodes, 1 to
.Dv CMC_MAX_NODES
(8).
.Fn init
sets a node's initial state.
.Pp
.Fn step
handles one event at one node.
It must be total and deterministic, and may read only its arguments: no
clock, randomness, globals, I/O or allocation.
It changes the state in place and emits effects with
.Fn cmc_out_push .
It must not change the first
.Fa durable_size
bytes; only
.Fn apply_persist ,
which the engine calls when a persist reaches disk, may change them.
A core with a non-zero
.Fa durable_size
must supply
.Fn apply_persist .
.Pp
.Fn clients ,
if set, says which nodes take client requests; it reads the settings,
never the state.
.Fn describe
and
.Fn describe_msg
print states and message bodies in traces.
.Fn direct_actions
and
.Fn describe_action
exist for calibration cores that port a shared-memory TLA+ specification
.Pq Xr cmc 7 ;
a message-passing core leaves them
.Dv NULL .
.Ss Events and effects
.Fn step
receives a
.Vt CmcEvent :
.Bd -literal
typedef struct CmcEvent {
	uint8_t	kind;		/* CmcEventKind */
	uint8_t	src;		/* RECV, CONN_RESET: the peer */
	uint16_t len;		/* RECV, FLUSHED: bytes in body */
	uint32_t arg;		/* TIMER, WAKE: the id; CLIENT: request number */
	CmcAction action;	/* ACTION (calibration only) */
	const uint8_t *body;	/* RECV: the message; FLUSHED: the record */
} CmcEvent;
.Ed
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width CMC_EV_CONN_RESET -compact
.It Dv CMC_EV_RECV
A message from
.Fa src .
.It Dv CMC_EV_TIMER
Timer
.Fa arg
fired.
.It Dv CMC_EV_FLUSHED
The persist record in
.Fa body
is now durable.
.It Dv CMC_EV_WAKE
Waiter
.Fa arg
was woken.
.It Dv CMC_EV_CLIENT
A client request,
.Fa arg
counting from 0 at this node.
.It Dv CMC_EV_RESTART
The node crashed: its volatile bytes are zeroed and it is starting
again.
.It Dv CMC_EV_CONN_RESET
The connection to
.Fa src
was reset, and the messages on it are gone.
.It Dv CMC_EV_ACTION
Calibration cores only.
.El
.Pp
.Fn cmc_out_push
appends an effect of the given kind to
.Fa out ,
zeroes it and returns it for the core to fill in.
.Bl -tag -width CMC_OUT_CANCEL_TIMER -compact
.It Dv CMC_OUT_SEND
Send
.Fa body
.Pq Fa len No bytes, at most Dv CMC_MSG_MAX , No 32
to
.Fa dst .
.It Dv CMC_OUT_SET_TIMER
Arm timer
.Fa arg ,
0 to 15.
.It Dv CMC_OUT_CANCEL_TIMER
Disarm timer
.Fa arg .
.It Dv CMC_OUT_PERSIST
Queue
.Fa body
as a disk write.
.It Dv CMC_OUT_WAKE
Queue a wake of waiter
.Fa arg ,
0 to 7.
.It Dv CMC_OUT_REPLY
Answer a client with
.Fa arg .
The engine appends the reply to the ghost log that properties read.
.El
.Pp
A core never writes
.Fa out->o
directly; the purity gate rejects source that does.
Past
.Dv CMC_OUT_MAX
(16) effects in one step,
.Fn cmc_out_push
returns a scratch entry and the engine reports the overflow as a
violation.
.Ss Properties
A property is a
.Vt CmcProp ,
made with one of the macros below from a name and a function.
State properties have the type
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bool fn(const CmcWorld *w, CmcWhy *why);
.Ed
.Pp
and action properties
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bool fn(const CmcWorld *pre, CmcAction a, const CmcWorld *post,
    CmcWhy *why);
.Ed
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width CMC_ACTION_PROPERTY -compact
.It Fn CMC_INVARIANT
Holds in every reachable state.
.It Fn CMC_ACTION_PROPERTY
Holds on every transition, including those to states already seen.
.It Fn CMC_WITNESS_PROP
Holds in some reachable state.
A witness never reached fails the run: it means the other properties
may hold only because the interesting states were never reached.
.It Fn CMC_QUIESCENT_PROP
Holds in every state where nothing can happen, or where the only
possible actions are timers that fire and change nothing.
.It Fn CMC_EVENTUALLY_PROP
Bounded liveness: from every reachable state, the fair schedule (no
faults, no new clients) reaches a state where it holds within
.Va live_steps
steps.
.El
.Pp
Each macro fills in a
.Vt CmcProp
whose kind is
.Dv CMC_INV ,
.Dv CMC_ACTION_PROP ,
.Dv CMC_WITNESS ,
.Dv CMC_QUIESCENT
or
.Dv CMC_EVENTUALLY .
.Pp
A property returns
.Dv false
to report a violation, and may explain it with
.Fn cmc_why ,
which formats like
.Xr printf 3 .
.Pp
Properties read the world through accessors.
.Fn cmc_node
returns node
.Fa node Ns 's
state and
.Fn cmc_cfg
the core's settings.
.Fn cmc_nreplies
and
.Fn cmc_reply
read the ghost log of client replies, in the order they were emitted.
.Fn cmc_requests
returns the number of client requests delivered to a node, counted by
the environment rather than by the core.
Properties may read core state; the engine never calls them to decide
which actions are possible.
.Ss Version
.Dv CMC_VERSION
is the release as a string,
.Ql MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH ,
following semantic versioning.
A change to
.In cmc.h
that breaks a core, a model or a caller written against an earlier
release of the same major version is not made outside a major release;
before 1.0.0, a minor release may make one, and
.Pa CHANGELOG.md
says so.
.Ss The model
.Bd -literal
typedef struct CmcModel {
	const char *name;
	const CmcCore *core;
	const CmcProp *props;
	int	nprops;
	int	nalways;	/* the first nalways props are always checked */
} CmcModel;

typedef struct CmcModelEntry {
	const char *name;	/* the --model name */
	const CmcModel *m;
} CmcModelEntry;
.Ed
.Ss Actions
A
.Vt CmcAction
is a 64-bit word.
.Fn CMC_ACT kind a b c d
packs one;
.Fn CMC_ACT_KIND ,
.Fn CMC_ACT_A ,
.Fn CMC_ACT_B ,
.Fn CMC_ACT_C
and
.Fn CMC_ACT_D
unpack its kind (the top byte), three byte fields and a 32-bit field.
An action property receives the action between its two worlds.
In a message-passing core the kind is one of
.Bl -tag -width CMC_A_DELIVER -compact
.It Dv CMC_A_DELIVER
a = destination, b = source, d = index of the message in the network.
.It Dv CMC_A_DROP
The same fields; the message is lost.
.It Dv CMC_A_DUP
The same fields; the message is duplicated.
.It Dv CMC_A_FIRE
a = node, b = timer.
.It Dv CMC_A_FLUSH
a = node: its oldest pending persist completes.
.It Dv CMC_A_WAKE
a = node, b = waiter.
.It Dv CMC_A_CLIENT
a = node.
.It Dv CMC_A_CRASH
a = node, b = how many pending persists reached disk.
.It Dv CMC_A_RESET
a = node, b = the peer whose connection was reset.
.El
.Pp
A calibration core defines its own kinds.
.Ss Options
.Bd -literal
typedef struct CmcOptions {
	CmcSearch search;	/* CMC_BFS, CMC_DFS, CMC_SIMULATE, CMC_REPLAY */
	int	max_depth;	/* DFS bound; simulation walk length */
	uint64_t seed;		/* simulation: first seed */
	uint64_t walks;		/* simulation: number of walks */
	uint64_t max_states;	/* 0: none; reaching it is incomplete */
	double	time_limit;	/* seconds; 0: none */
	bool	det;		/* determinism gate */
	bool	stop_on_witness; /* stop once every witness is reached */
	bool	quiet;		/* print no trace or progress */
	bool	coverage;	/* count states per action kind */
	int	progress_s;	/* progress line period; 0: off */
	const char *trace_out;	/* write a replay file on a violation */
	const char *replay_in;	/* CMC_REPLAY: the file */
	int	client_budget, drop_budget, dup_budget, crash_budget;
	int	net_cap, persist_cap, reply_cap;
	CmcNet	net;		/* CMC_NET_FIFO or CMC_NET_BAG */
	int	live_steps;	/* bound for eventually-properties */
	FILE	*out;		/* progress output; NULL: stdout */
} CmcOptions;
.Ed
.Pp
The fields are the options of
.Xr cmc 1 ,
which gives their defaults.
.Ss Running a check
.Fn cmc_main
parses the command line described in
.Xr cmc 1 ,
runs the check, prints TLC-style output, and returns the verdict, which
the caller returns from
.Fn main .
.Pp
To drive the engine directly, fill a
.Vt CmcOptions
with
.Fn cmc_options_default ,
change what is needed, and call
.Fn cmc_run_new
with the model, a settings string
.Ql key=value,...
and a
.Dv NULL Ns -terminated
list of property names, or
.Dv NULL
for all of them.
On failure it returns
.Dv NULL
and writes the reason to
.Fa err .
.Pp
.Fn cmc_check
runs the search and fills
.Fa res .
On a violation,
.Fa res->prop
names the property
.Po
.Ql cmc:engine
for a broken engine rule
.Pc ,
.Fa res->why
explains it, and
.Fa res->trace
holds the
.Fa res->trace_len No \- 1
actions from the initial state.
.Fn cmc_print_trace
prints them state by state, and
.Fn cmc_write_replay
saves them in the format
.Fl -replay
reads.
.Fn cmc_result_free
frees the trace;
.Fn cmc_run_free
frees the run.
.Pp
.Fn cmc_world_size
returns the bytes in one world: every node's state plus the environment.
.Fn cmc_describe_action
prints one action.
.Ss Lower level
.Fn cmc_world_init
writes the initial world into
.Fa w ,
which holds
.Fn cmc_world_size
bytes.
.Fn cmc_enabled
lists the actions possible in
.Fa w
and returns their number, or \-1 if there are more than
.Fa max .
.Fn cmc_apply
applies one action in place.
.Fn cmc_fingerprint
is the 128-bit hash the visited-state table uses.
These exist for the engine's own tests.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn cmc_main
returns a
.Vt CmcVerdict :
.Dv CMC_PASS
(0),
.Dv CMC_VIOLATION
(1),
.Dv CMC_INCOMPLETE
(2) or
.Dv CMC_ERROR
(3), the exit statuses listed in
.Xr cmc 1 .
.Pp
.Fn cmc_run_new
returns
.Dv NULL
on a bad setting, an unknown property, a bound out of range, a
durable part without
.Fn apply_persist ,
or a duplicating FIFO network.
.Fn cmc_apply
returns 0, or \-1 if the action is not possible or a core broke an
engine rule.
.Fn cmc_write_replay
returns 0, or \-1 if the file cannot be written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A complete model, with the core, two properties and
.Fn main ,
is in
.Pa docs/_includes/snippets/quickstart.c
in the source tree.
The skeleton:
.Bd -literal
#include "cmc.h"

static const CmcCore my_core = {
	.name = "mine",
	.state_size = sizeof(MyState),
	.durable_size = offsetof(MyState, first_volatile),
	.cfg_default = my_cfg_default,
	.cfg_set = my_cfg_set,
	.nnodes = my_nnodes,
	.init = my_init,
	.step = my_step,
	.apply_persist = my_apply_persist,
};

static const CmcProp my_props[] = {
	CMC_INVARIANT(NoLostAck, no_lost_ack),
	CMC_WITNESS_PROP(Acked, acked),
};

static const CmcModel my_model = {
	.name = "mine", .core = &my_core,
	.props = my_props, .nprops = 2,
};

int
main(int argc, char **argv)
{
	static const CmcModelEntry models[] = {
		{"mine", &my_model},
	};

	return cmc_main(argc, argv, models, 1);
}
.Ed
.Pp
Build it against the library:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cc -std=c11 -Ilibcmc/include mine.c mine_core.o \e
    libcmc/build/libcmc.a -o mycmc
.Ed
.Sh LIMITS
.Bl -tag -width CMC_MAX_ACTIONS -compact
.It Dv CMC_MAX_NODES
8 nodes.
.It Dv CMC_MSG_MAX
32 bytes per message or persist record.
.It Dv CMC_OUT_MAX
16 effects per step.
.It Dv CMC_MAX_ACTIONS
2048 possible actions per state.
.It Dv CMC_MAX_TIMERS
16 timers per node.
.It Dv CMC_MAX_WAKES
8 waiters per node.
.El
.Pp
Going past a limit is reported as a violation, never truncated.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmc 1 ,
.Xr cmc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
The library is C11 and uses only libc.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Greg Burd Aq Mt greg@burd.me
.Sh BUGS
The library is single-threaded and has no symmetry reduction; the
visited set and the search queue live in memory.
